---
// MethodDiagram.astro
// ONE-claim hero diagram for the Semantic Canvas / thesis mechanism:
//   image + axis-text share ONE CLIP space  →  position = a single dot product.
// Inline SVG so it inherits the page CSS vars: neutrals use currentColor +
// surface vars, the single focal accent uses rgb(var(--accent-rgb)). This
// themes light/dark automatically with no -light twin needed.
// Rebuilt 2026-07 to the 5-second-gist bar (was a 5-stage, ~30-label spec).
---

<figure class="my-12">
  <div
    class="rounded-md border border-graphite-700/60 bg-[rgb(var(--surface-1-rgb))] p-6 md:p-10"
  >
    <svg
      viewBox="0 0 1160 380"
      role="img"
      aria-labelledby="method-diagram-title"
      class="w-full h-auto text-[rgb(var(--text-secondary))]"
      xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
      font-family="'IBM Plex Mono', ui-monospace, monospace"
    >
      <title id="method-diagram-title">
        Semantic Canvas mechanism: image and axis-text share one CLIP space; position is one dot product.
      </title>

      <defs>
        <marker id="md-arrow" markerWidth="9" markerHeight="9" refX="7" refY="4.5" orient="auto">
          <path d="M0,0 L8,4.5 L0,9 Z" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.5" />
        </marker>
      </defs>

      {/* title */}
      <text x="40" y="40" fill="rgb(var(--accent-rgb))" font-size="16" letter-spacing="3">THE MECHANISM</text>
      <text x="40" y="64" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.6" font-size="13">One embedding space · one dot product · no training</text>

      {/* input: image */}
      <g>
        <rect x="40" y="120" width="70" height="70" rx="6" fill="rgb(var(--surface-2-rgb))" stroke="currentColor" stroke-opacity="0.25"/>
        <rect x="52" y="132" width="70" height="70" rx="6" fill="rgb(var(--surface-2-rgb))" stroke="currentColor" stroke-opacity="0.4"/>
        <rect x="64" y="144" width="70" height="70" rx="6" fill="rgb(var(--surface-2-rgb))" stroke="currentColor" stroke-opacity="0.7"/>
        <text x="99" y="238" text-anchor="middle" fill="currentColor" font-size="13">Project image</text>
      </g>

      {/* input: axis text */}
      <g>
        <rect x="34" y="278" width="200" height="56" rx="6" fill="rgb(var(--surface-2-rgb))" stroke="currentColor" stroke-opacity="0.5"/>
        <text x="134" y="302" text-anchor="middle" fill="currentColor" font-size="14">“casual ↔ formal”</text>
        <text x="134" y="320" text-anchor="middle" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.55" font-size="10.5">you type an axis</text>
      </g>

      {/* arrows into CLIP */}
      <g fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-opacity="0.45" stroke-width="1.6">
        <path d="M140,178 L326,196" marker-end="url(#md-arrow)"/>
        <path d="M240,300 L326,236" marker-end="url(#md-arrow)"/>
      </g>

      {/* CLIP encoder — shared space */}
      <rect x="330" y="150" width="216" height="120" rx="7" fill="rgb(var(--surface-2-rgb))" stroke="currentColor" stroke-opacity="0.55"/>
      <text x="438" y="196" text-anchor="middle" fill="currentColor" font-size="16">OpenCLIP ViT-L/14</text>
      <text x="438" y="220" text-anchor="middle" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.6" font-size="12">768-D shared space</text>
      <text x="438" y="244" text-anchor="middle" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.45" font-size="10.5">one model · image + text</text>

      {/* arrow to dot product */}
      <path d="M546,210 L604,210" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-opacity="0.45" stroke-width="1.6" marker-end="url(#md-arrow)"/>

      {/* dot product — THE focal element (oxide) */}
      <rect x="606" y="160" width="150" height="100" rx="7" fill="rgb(var(--accent-rgb) / 0.12)" stroke="rgb(var(--accent-rgb))" stroke-width="1.5"/>
      <text x="681" y="205" text-anchor="middle" fill="rgb(var(--accent-rgb))" font-size="26">v · â</text>
      <text x="681" y="230" text-anchor="middle" fill="rgb(var(--accent-rgb))" font-size="12" letter-spacing="1">DOT PRODUCT</text>

      {/* annotation — the one 'so what' */}
      <text x="681" y="302" text-anchor="middle" fill="rgb(var(--accent-rgb))" font-size="12.5">No training — a new axis is free.</text>
      <text x="681" y="320" text-anchor="middle" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.5" font-size="10.5">O(N · D), instant re-projection</text>

      {/* arrow to canvas */}
      <path d="M756,210 L826,210" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-opacity="0.45" stroke-width="1.6" marker-end="url(#md-arrow)"/>

      {/* output: 2-D canvas */}
      <g>
        <rect x="830" y="120" width="220" height="180" rx="7" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-opacity="0.5"/>
        <line x1="852" y1="284" x2="1034" y2="284" stroke="currentColor" stroke-opacity="0.35"/>
        <line x1="852" y1="284" x2="852" y2="140" stroke="currentColor" stroke-opacity="0.35"/>
        <circle cx="892" cy="250" r="4.5" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.6"/>
        <circle cx="930" cy="205" r="4.5" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.6"/>
        <circle cx="978" cy="228" r="4.5" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.6"/>
        <circle cx="1002" cy="175" r="4.5" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.6"/>
        <circle cx="956" cy="160" r="6" fill="rgb(var(--accent-rgb))"/>
        <text x="940" y="326" text-anchor="middle" fill="currentColor" font-size="13">2-D canvas</text>
      </g>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption class="mono-label mt-3">
    The mechanism · An image and a typed axis land in one CLIP space; their dot product is the coordinate — adding an axis needs no training.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
